  "definition": "Intracranial stimulation is a research procedure in which electrodes are implanted in the brain and used to deliver electrical stimulation to a specific region. In the cited study, stimulation of the dorsal periaqueductal gray was used in adult rats to evoke and examine panic-like behaviors.",
